In FGCP the new primary takes over the cluster's virtual MAC addresses, so neighbours keep using the same gateway IP;
with session pickup on, established TCP sessions survive. Document the test result in the acceptance report with the
output of `get system ha status` before and after.

An SLA rule uses the first member in priority order that meets the SLA. Probing the ERP itself through each
tunnel measures what users experience end to end, ISP and tunnel included. Probes leave from the member's IP;
a tunnel without one needs `source`, or HQ's reverse-path check drops the probe (it would come from the WAN IP).
